w-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","attempt":1},"attempts":[{"number":1,"status":"changes_requested","preparationKind":"planning","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"06cdafb3c2a74866d45e5cbef4ff5c4293b28ef06b2321f5959b140534da6c90","document":"0308c75a6c18c2074057b90edc15f5b8ba2958f2ead932f39412ad95e603601f"},"contentIdentity":"6996712e984d5e22efa53d603e2a364cda1cbb59f469f63a76f9b7dea57305da","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794338808202-hv8d1c\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-10T19:29:54.698Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-10T19:29:54.698Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"unknown\",\n          \"model\": \"unknown\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 186065,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"e0821209d94791d0\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794338808202-hv8d1c\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"e0821209d94791d007c3006b8a60474b83ec57720d3cfedcddbf3fbf7472a3d9\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Move new-chat out of the history dropdown into an icon button left of the history widget\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"small\",\n    \"triageRationale\": \"One webview module, one obvious approach: the history menu trailing new… row is removed and a dedicated button is placed before .histchip, reusing the .pico icon slot and the existing newChatPick() message; the host new-chat contract is untouched. Two files change: chat-panel.ts and chat-panel.test.ts.\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"lifecycle\": {\n      \"status\": \"draft\",\n      \"revision\": {\n        \"number\": 1,\n        \"contentHash\": \"993857e1751e29d9f26a8ef584e0283705d2b35566837dfa2499216fbc48a615\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-10T19:29:54.835Z\",\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"insrc:system\",\n          \"kind\": \"system\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"signoffs\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 1\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"prose\": \"This story moves the chat panel's new-chat action out of the history dropdown menu and into a dedicated icon button sitting immediately left of the history widget in the chrome bar. The button carries a chat-bubble-with-plus glyph and posts the exact same new-chat message as before, so session creation and all host-side handling are untouched; only the webview trigger and its pinning tests change.\",\n      \"audience\": \"technical\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Move new-chat out of the history dropdown into an icon button left of the history widget\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"VS Code chat webview shell (vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts): the .chrome header's right-aligned cluster (.right > #insrc-newchat button + .histchip > #insrc-history + #insrc-histmenu popup). The history menu becomes a pure session list; new-chat is a first-class chrome button. No change to the host message protocol, the session store, or provider adapters.\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"renderHistoryMenu\",\n          \"signature\": \"() => void — rebuilds #insrc-histmenu rows from histEntries (webview bootstrap function in the nonce'd shell script)\",\n          \"parameters\": [],\n          \"returns\": \"void (mutates #insrc-histmenu children: one mitem row per histEntries entry, no trailing row)\",\n          \"errors\": [\n            \"none — DOM-only; an empty histEntries yields an empty menu\"\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"histMenu element exists in the shell\",\n            \"histEntries populated from history-list messages\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"#insrc-histmenu contains exactly one role=menuitem row per persisted chat and NO 'new…' row (the row this story removes)\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"newChatPick\",\n          \"signature\": \"newChatPick(trigger: HTMLElement | null) => void — closes popups, refocuses trigger, posts the new-chat message (webview bootstrap function)\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"trigger\",\n              \"type\": \"HTMLElement | null\",\n              \"purpose\": \"element to refocus after posting (the #insrc-newchat button)\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": \"void (side effect: vs.postMessage)\",\n          \"errors\": [\n            \"none\"\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"vs message channel open\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"posts {v:1, payload:{type:'new-chat', provider: curProv || ''}} — identical payload to the old menu row, so the host's new-chat handler is unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"#insrc-newchat click listener\",\n          \"signature\": \"(click on the chrome button) => stopPropagation(); newChatPick(nc) — new wiring added by this story\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"event\",\n              \"type\": \"MouseEvent\",\n              \"purpose\": \"stopPropagation so document click-close does not race the post\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": \"void\",\n          \"errors\": [\n            \"none — native <button> also fires click on Enter/Space, giving keyboard activation without extra handlers\"\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"#insrc-newchat exists in the shell markup (placed before .histchip in .right)\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"popups closed, new-chat posted, button keeps focus\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"ChatSession / history-list / new-chat message envelope\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"No persisted or protocol change: the new-chat payload {type:'new-chat', provider} is byte-identical, history-list is unchanged, and no store schema is touched. The only data change is presentational: the history menu's row set loses its synthetic 'new…' entry.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2564\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2568\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2751\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2337\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"User clicks #insrc-newchat while a history/active popup is open\",\n          \"detection\": \"the button's own click listener stopPropagation()s before document click-close runs; newChatPick then calls closePops() itself\",\n          \"response\": \"all popups close, new-chat is posted once, focus moves to the button\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"none — single new-chat post, no double-fire\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Host rejects the new-chat (e.g. cross-provider new-chat on a started session)\",\n          \"detection\": \"host refuses and re-echoes run-config/history-list; webview reconcile() snaps selections back to cur (existing behavior at chat-panel.ts:2562)\",\n          \"response\": \"webview state unchanged; no menu row involved anymore\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"same as before the change — the refusal path is host-side and untouched\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"empty history list (no persisted chats yet)\",\n          \"expected\": \"history menu opens with zero rows (no 'new…' row anymore); the #insrc-newchat button remains the only new-chat affordance and works identically\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"keyboard user focuses #insrc-newchat and presses Enter/Space\",\n          \"expected\": \"native <button> fires click -> newChatPick(nc) posts new-chat; no custom key handler needed\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Escape while focus is on #insrc-newchat\",\n          \"expected\": \"document keydown closes popups (closePops); button is not a popup trigger, nothing else happens\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"CSP of the webview\",\n          \"expected\": \"inline SVG in static shell markup is allowed (same mechanism as PROVIDER_ICON_SVGS); the icon renders with currentColor\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The new-chat message payload {type:'new-chat', provider: curProv||''} is unchanged, so the host's session-creation handler and all env('new-chat') host tests keep passing.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The history trigger's empty label stays 'new…' (renderTriggers) — only the MENU row is removed, not the chip label.\",\n          \"source\": \"c3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"closePops() still closes every popup and clears aria-expanded on both triggers; the new button needs no popup state.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testFramework\": \"node:test + assert/strict via npx tsx --test, with the panel's fidelityHtml() shell snapshot and fakeChannel() host-message capture (existing chat-panel.test.ts conventions)\",\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Pin the shell markup and bootstrap wiring for the relocated new-chat trigger and the row-less history menu.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — update the 'regression: the history trigger still opens/new-chats…' test (lines ~2011-2021): newChatPick still posts {type:'new-chat',provider:curProv||''}, now triggered by the #insrc-newchat click listener; renderHistoryMenu output contains no 'new…'/'starts a new chat' row\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — update the '#insrc-history session dropdown' markup test (line ~2337): .right contains <button id=\\\"insrc-newchat\\\"> BEFORE <span class=\\\"histchip\\\">; the button carries the bubble-plus SVG in its .pico slot and aria-label/title 'new chat'\",\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — add assertions: doesNotMatch 'starts a new chat'; match on id=\\\"insrc-newchat\\\" click wiring calling newChatPick; match on the bubble path + plus strokes of the icon SVG\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"fidelityHtml() snapshot (existing)\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Prove the host contract is unchanged: env('new-chat', ...) host tests still pass unmodified.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — existing new-chat host tests (lines 229, 648, 659, 735, 792, 869, 1101, 1144, 1573, 3514, 3952, 4431, 4505, 4524, 4619) run unchanged\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"fakeChannel() + createChatPanelHost with scriptedAdapter (existing)\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"updated history-trigger regression test: doesNotMatch /starts a new chat/ in renderHistoryMenu; history menu rows = histEntries only\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"markup test: /<button type=\\\"button\\\" id=\\\"insrc-newchat\\\"[^>]*><span class=\\\"pico\\\">/ appears before /<span class=\\\"histchip\\\">/ in the .right span\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"markup test: the #insrc-newchat .pico contains the inline bubble-plus SVG (bubble path + two plus strokes), fill/stroke currentColor\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac4\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"wiring test: /insrc-newchat/ listener calls newChatPick and newChatPick posts /type:'new-chat',provider:curProv\\\\|\\\\|''/; all existing env('new-chat') host tests pass unchanged\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac5\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"full suite: npx tsx --test vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts passes (plus cli-adapter.test.ts), tsc --noEmit clean\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"The chat chrome's .right cluster contains only the .histchip history widget; its dropdown menu (#insrc-histmenu) ends with a synthetic 'new…' / 'starts a new chat' row that posts {type:'new-chat'} via newChatPick (chat-panel.ts:2568). No dedicated new-chat button exists in the chrome.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"The history menu lists only persisted chats (no 'new…' row), and a dedicated icon button #insrc-newchat sits immediately left of .histchip in .right, carrying a chat-bubble-plus inline SVG and posting the identical {type:'new-chat', provider: curProv||''} message on click (native button keyboard semantics). Host, store and message protocol unchanged.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Add the #insrc-newchat button markup before .histchip in .chrome .right with the bubble-plus SVG in a .pico slot, plus .newchatbtn CSS (chip-matching ground/border/radius, hover/focus-visible states)\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Wire the button's click listener (stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc)) in the bootstrap script and remove the trailing mitem row from renderHistoryMenu\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Update the two pinning tests in chat-panel.test.ts (history-trigger regression test, histchip markup test) and add assertions for the button placement, icon, wiring and the row-less menu\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"Fully backward compatible: the new-chat webview->host message payload is byte-identical, history-list is unchanged, no persisted schema exists for the chrome, and all host-side env('new-chat') tests pass unmodified. Older webview shells are not persisted (the shell is rebuilt on every panel open), so there is no mixed-version state.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": true,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": false\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Icon button left of the history chip (chosen shape)\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"A real <button id=insrc-newchat> in .chrome .right immediately before .histchip; click posts the unchanged {type:'new-chat'} via newChatPick; the history menu loses its trailing 'new…' row.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Markup: insert the button into the .right span before the histchip (chat-panel.ts:2751). CSS: a compact bordered icon button reusing the chip's ground/border/radius and the existing .pico 14px slot for a bubble-plus inline SVG (currentColor). JS: const nc=getElementById('insrc-newchat'); nc click -> stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc); renderHistoryMenu drops the appended mitem row. Native <button> gives Enter/Space activation and focus for free; aria-label/title 'new chat'.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Matches the requested UX exactly (button left of the history widget, bubble-plus icon)\",\n          \"Message contract {type:'new-chat'} and all host handling unchanged — zero host-side diff\",\n          \"Reuses existing primitives (.pico slot, .histchip look, newChatPick, closePops)\",\n          \"Keyboard accessible via native button semantics\",\n          \"Smallest diff that fully meets the story\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"One more control in the chrome row (space is ample — .right is right-aligned with the actchip on the left)\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"XS\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Keep the row, add a header button too (dual affordance)\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Add the icon button left of .histchip but ALSO keep the 'new…' row at the bottom of the history menu.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Same as a1 for the button, plus renderHistoryMenu keeps its trailing mitem row.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Two ways to discover new-chat\",\n          \"Smaller test churn (old row assertions stay)\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Duplicates the action in two places — exactly what the story asks to remove\",\n          \"Menu still carries a non-history row\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"XS\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Violates the primary requirement — keeps the duplicated 'new…' row the story asks to remove\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"name\": \"Icon button inside the input bar\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Place the new-chat button at the left edge of .inputbar next to the ❯ prompt instead of the chrome.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Markup in the .inputbar div; same click wiring; history menu row removed.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Keeps the chrome single-purpose\",\n          \"Near the primary input affordance\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Moves the action away from the history widget the story names\",\n          \"Crowds the input bar; the ❯ prompt already lives there\",\n          \"Bigger CSS/layout risk for no gain\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"S\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Places the button in the input bar instead of left of the history widget; adds layout risk\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a4\",\n        \"name\": \"Status quo (row only)\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Keep the trailing 'new…' row in the history menu; change nothing.\",\n        \"approach\": \"No change.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Zero cost\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Does not meet the story at all — the row at the bottom of the history list is the behavior being removed\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"XS\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"No change at all — does not meet the story\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": []\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2526-2590\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"bootstrap JS wiring: hs=#insrc-history, renderHistoryMenu with the trailing new… row, newChatPick posting {type:'new-chat',provider:curProv||''}, closePops\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2747-2752\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"chrome markup: .right > .histchip > #insrc-history button + #insrc-histmenu popup — the placement point for the new button\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018\",\n      \"quotedText\": \"pinning assertions for newChatPick/'new…' row and the histchip markup (line 2337) that this story updates\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2282-2283\",\n      \"quotedText\": \".pico{...14px...} .pico svg{width:14px;height:14px;display:block;} — the icon slot the bubble-plus SVG reuses\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-e0821209d94791d0-s1 — Move new-chat out of the history dropdown into an icon button left of the history widget\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794338808202-hv8d1c`\n**HLD effective hash:** `e0821209d947...`\n\nThis story moves the chat panel's new-chat action out of the history dropdown menu and into a dedicated icon button sitting immediately left of the history widget in the chrome bar. The button carries a chat-bubble-with-plus glyph and posts the exact same new-chat message as before, so session creation and all host-side handling are untouched; only the webview trigger and its pinning tests change.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Error paths](#4-error-paths)\n5. [Test strategy](#5-test-strategy)\n6. [Migration](#6-migration)\n7. [Alternatives considered](#7-alternatives-considered)\n8. [References](#8-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** VS Code chat webview shell (vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts): the .chrome header's right-aligned cluster (.right > #insrc-newchat button + .histchip > #insrc-history + #insrc-histmenu popup). The history menu becomes a pure session list; new-chat is a first-class chrome button. No change to the host message protocol, the session store, or provider adapters.\n\n### 2.1 `renderHistoryMenu`\n\n```typescript\n() => void — rebuilds #insrc-histmenu rows from histEntries (webview bootstrap function in the nonce'd shell script)\n```\n\n**Returns:** `undefined` — undefined\n\n**Errors:**\n- `undefined` when undefined\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- histMenu element exists in the shell\n- histEntries populated from history-list messages\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- #insrc-histmenu contains exactly one role=menuitem row per persisted chat and NO 'new…' row (the row this story removes)\n\n### 2.2 `newChatPick`\n\n```typescript\nnewChatPick(trigger: HTMLElement | null) => void — closes popups, refocuses trigger, posts the new-chat message (webview bootstrap function)\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `trigger: HTMLElement | null` — element to refocus after posting (the #insrc-newchat button)\n\n**Returns:** `undefined` — undefined\n\n**Errors:**\n- `undefined` when undefined\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- vs message channel open\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- posts {v:1, payload:{type:'new-chat', provider: curProv || ''}} — identical payload to the old menu row, so the host's new-chat handler is unchanged\n\n### 2.3 `#insrc-newchat click listener`\n\n```typescript\n(click on the chrome button) => stopPropagation(); newChatPick(nc) — new wiring added by this story\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `event: MouseEvent` — stopPropagation so document click-close does not race the post\n\n**Returns:** `undefined` — undefined\n\n**Errors:**\n- `undefined` when undefined\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- #insrc-newchat exists in the shell markup (placed before .histchip in .right)\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- popups closed, new-chat posted, button keeps focus\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `ChatSession / history-list / new-chat message envelope` — invariant-change\n\nNo persisted or protocol change: the new-chat payload {type:'new-chat', provider} is byte-identical, history-list is unchanged, and no store schema is touched. The only data change is presentational: the history menu's row set loses its synthetic 'new…' entry.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2564`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2568`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2751`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2337`\n\n## 4. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **User clicks #insrc-newchat while a history/active popup is open** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: the button's own click listener stopPropagation()s before document click-close runs; newChatPick then calls closePops() itself\n  - Response: all popups close, new-chat is posted once, focus moves to the button\n  - User impact: none — single new-chat post, no double-fire\n- **Host rejects the new-chat (e.g. cross-provider new-chat on a started session)** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: host refuses and re-echoes run-config/history-list; webview reconcile() snaps selections back to cur (existing behavior at chat-panel.ts:2562)\n  - Response: webview state unchanged; no menu row involved anymore\n  - User impact: same as before the change — the refusal path is host-side and untouched\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| empty history list (no persisted chats yet) | history menu opens with zero rows (no 'new…' row anymore); the #insrc-newchat button remains the only new-chat affordance and works identically |\n| keyboard user focuses #insrc-newchat and presses Enter/Space | native <button> fires click -> newChatPick(nc) posts new-chat; no custom key handler needed |\n| Escape while focus is on #insrc-newchat | document keydown closes popups (closePops); button is not a popup trigger, nothing else happens |\n| CSP of the webview | inline SVG in static shell markup is allowed (same mechanism as PROVIDER_ICON_SVGS); the icon renders with currentColor |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- The new-chat message payload {type:'new-chat', provider: curProv||''} is unchanged, so the host's session-creation handler and all env('new-chat') host tests keep passing. [[c1]]\n- The history trigger's empty label stays 'new…' (renderTriggers) — only the MENU row is removed, not the chip label. [[c3]]\n- closePops() still closes every popup and clears aria-expanded on both triggers; the new button needs no popup state. [[c1]]\n\n## 5. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `node:test + assert/strict via npx tsx --test, with the panel's fidelityHtml() shell snapshot and fakeChannel() host-message capture (existing chat-panel.test.ts conventions)`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — Pin the shell markup and bootstrap wiring for the relocated new-chat trigger and the row-less history menu.\n  - Subjects: `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — update the 'regression: the history trigger still opens/new-chats…' test (lines ~2011-2021): newChatPick still posts {type:'new-chat',provider:curProv||''}, now triggered by the #insrc-newchat click listener; renderHistoryMenu output contains no 'new…'/'starts a new chat' row`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — update the '#insrc-history session dropdown' markup test (line ~2337): .right contains <button id=\"insrc-newchat\"> BEFORE <span class=\"histchip\">; the button carries the bubble-plus SVG in its .pico slot and aria-label/title 'new chat'`, `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — add assertions: doesNotMatch 'starts a new chat'; match on id=\"insrc-newchat\" click wiring calling newChatPick; match on the bubble path + plus strokes of the icon SVG`\n  - Fixtures: `fidelityHtml() snapshot (existing)`\n- **integration** — Prove the host contract is unchanged: env('new-chat', ...) host tests still pass unmodified.\n  - Subjects: `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts — existing new-chat host tests (lines 229, 648, 659, 735, 792, 869, 1101, 1144, 1573, 3514, 3952, 4431, 4505, 4524, 4619) run unchanged`\n  - Fixtures: `fakeChannel() + createChatPanelHost with scriptedAdapter (existing)`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `updated history-trigger regression test: doesNotMatch /starts a new chat/ in renderHistoryMenu; history menu rows = histEntries only` |\n| `ac2` | `markup test: /<button type=\"button\" id=\"insrc-newchat\"[^>]*><span class=\"pico\">/ appears before /<span class=\"histchip\">/ in the .right span` |\n| `ac3` | `markup test: the #insrc-newchat .pico contains the inline bubble-plus SVG (bubble path + two plus strokes), fill/stroke currentColor` |\n| `ac4` | `wiring test: /insrc-newchat/ listener calls newChatPick and newChatPick posts /type:'new-chat',provider:curProv\\|\\|''/; all existing env('new-chat') host tests pass unchanged` |\n| `ac5` | `full suite: npx tsx --test vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts passes (plus cli-adapter.test.ts), tsc --noEmit clean` |\n\n## 6. Migration\n\n**State before:** The chat chrome's .right cluster contains only the .histchip history widget; its dropdown menu (#insrc-histmenu) ends with a synthetic 'new…' / 'starts a new chat' row that posts {type:'new-chat'} via newChatPick (chat-panel.ts:2568). No dedicated new-chat button exists in the chrome.\n\n**State after:** The history menu lists only persisted chats (no 'new…' row), and a dedicated icon button #insrc-newchat sits immediately left of .histchip in .right, carrying a chat-bubble-plus inline SVG and posting the identical {type:'new-chat', provider: curProv||''} message on click (native button keyboard semantics). Host, store and message protocol unchanged.\n\n**Zero downtime:** yes — **Data rewrite:** no\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Add the #insrc-newchat button markup before .histchip in .chrome .right with the bubble-plus SVG in a .pico slot, plus .newchatbtn CSS (chip-matching ground/border/radius, hover/focus-visible states) — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Wire the button's click listener (stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc)) in the bootstrap script and remove the trailing mitem row from renderHistoryMenu — ↩ rollbackable\n3. Update the two pinning tests in chat-panel.test.ts (history-trigger regression test, histchip markup test) and add assertions for the button placement, icon, wiring and the row-less menu — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** Fully backward compatible: the new-chat webview->host message payload is byte-identical, history-list is unchanged, no persisted schema exists for the chrome, and all host-side env('new-chat') tests pass unmodified. Older webview shells are not persisted (the shell is rebuilt on every panel open), so there is no mixed-version state.\n\n## 7. Alternatives considered\n\n### 7.1 a1: Icon button left of the history chip (chosen shape) — **CHOSEN**\n\nA real <button id=insrc-newchat> in .chrome .right immediately before .histchip; click posts the unchanged {type:'new-chat'} via newChatPick; the history menu loses its trailing 'new…' row.\n\nMarkup: insert the button into the .right span before the histchip (chat-panel.ts:2751). CSS: a compact bordered icon button reusing the chip's ground/border/radius and the existing .pico 14px slot for a bubble-plus inline SVG (currentColor). JS: const nc=getElementById('insrc-newchat'); nc click -> stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc); renderHistoryMenu drops the appended mitem row. Native <button> gives Enter/Space activation and focus for free; aria-label/title 'new chat'.\n\n### 7.2 a2: Keep the row, add a header button too (dual affordance)\n\nAdd the icon button left of .histchip but ALSO keep the 'new…' row at the bottom of the history menu.\n\nSame as a1 for the button, plus renderHistoryMenu keeps its trailing mitem row.\n\n**Rejected because:** Violates the primary requirement — keeps the duplicated 'new…' row the story asks to remove\n\n### 7.3 a3: Icon button inside the input bar\n\nPlace the new-chat button at the left edge of .inputbar next to the ❯ prompt instead of the chrome.\n\nMarkup in the .inputbar div; same click wiring; history menu row removed.\n\n**Rejected because:** Places the button in the input bar instead of left of the history widget; adds layout risk\n\n### 7.4 a4: Status quo (row only)\n\nKeep the trailing 'new…' row in the history menu; change nothing.\n\nNo change.\n\n**Rejected because:** No change at all — does not meet the story\n\n## 8. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2526-2590` — \"bootstrap JS wiring: hs=#insrc-history, renderHistoryMenu with the trailing new… row, newChatPick posting {type:'new-chat',provider:curProv||''}, closePops\"\n- **[[c2]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2747-2752` — \"chrome markup: .right > .histchip > #insrc-history button + #insrc-histmenu popup — the placement point for the new button\"\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018` — \"pinning assertions for newChatPick/'new…' row and the histchip markup (line 2337) that this story updates\"\n- **[[c4]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2282-2283` — \".pico{...14px...} .pico svg{width:14px;height:14px;display:block;} — the icon slot the bubble-plus SVG reuses\"\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-10T19:30:10.151Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/summary","title":"summary","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/contractDetails","selector":"/body/contractDetails","title":"contractDetails","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/dataModelChanges","selector":"/body/dataModelChanges","title":"dataModelChanges","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/interactionWithShared","selector":"/body/interactionWithShared","title":"interactionWithShared","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/errorPaths","selector":"/body/errorPaths","title":"errorPaths","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/testStrategy","selector":"/body/testStrategy","title":"testStrategy","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/migration","selector":"/body/migration","title":"migration","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered","title":"alternativesConsidered","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/chosenAlternative","selector":"/body/chosenAlternative","title":"chosenAlternative","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/openQuestions","selector":"/body/openQuestions","title":"openQuestions","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","title":"a1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","title":"a2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","title":"a3","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","selector":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","title":"a4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:24","selector":"document:line:24","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"ch1-scope","status":"passed","summary":"The standalone framing is correctly justified and matches the story's actual scope (a two-file, single-webview-module change with no cross-story contracts). interactionWithShared=[] and openQuestions=[] are both defensible: the change only reuses existing shared primitives (.pico icon slot, chip-matching CSS values) without modifying their definitions, and the one cross-file test surface that renders the same chrome markup (chat-shell.test.ts) still passes under the new markup by inspection. The summary's claim that \"only the webview trigger and its pinning tests change\" is consistent with the detailed sections — the new button's markup/CSS/icon/wiring are all part of implementing that trigger, and the host/store/protocol are untouched. Two minor LOW-level observations are noted as advice, not blocking.","findings":[{"id":"f1-hld-metadata-confusing","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/summary (document:line:7-9)","message":"The Summary section states a concrete 'HLD base run' id and 'HLD effective hash' immediately above the explicit statement in section 1 (document:line:26) that this is a 'Standalone feature — no parent HLD.' Carrying real-looking HLD hash fields for a story that has no HLD is consistent with how the framework self-stamps standalone runs (meta.standalone=true, meta.hldBaseRunId===meta.runId), but the juxtaposition could mislead a reader into thinking an actual HLD artifact was authored and consulted.","evidenceReferences":["document:line:7","document:line:8","document:line:9","document:line:24","document:line:26",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json#meta.standalone",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json#meta.hldBaseRunId"]},{"id":"f2-chat-shell-test-not-mentioned","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/interactionWithShared","message":"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts renders the same chrome shell (runShell()) and contains an assertion at its 'E202611031bd72813:S001 t4' test that locates 'class=\"right\"' and 'id=\"insrc-history\"' by string index and asserts histAt > rightAt. Inserting the new #insrc-newchat button inside .right before .histchip does not break this specific assertion (histAt is still after the '.right' span open), so no fix is required, but this cross-file shared-rendering surface is not mentioned anywhere in interactionWithShared, dataModelChanges.callSites, or the test strategy's subjects, despite being the one other place in the repo that renders and pins the same .right/.histchip markup this story changes.","evidenceReferences":["vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts:717-724","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2751","/body/interactionWithShared"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2500-2799","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2260-2299","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts:705-734",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider a one-line note in interactionWithShared (even for a standalone story) naming chat-shell.test.ts as a verified-unaffected shared rendering surface, so future readers don't have to re-derive that the index-based assertion still holds after the markup insertion.","Since the exact bubble-plus SVG path data is not pinned anywhere in the LLD (only described verbally), the builder has latitude in the literal icon markup; this is fine for a UI-only change but could be called out explicitly as a deliberately-deferred implementation detail rather than left implicit."]},{"chunkId":"ch2-contract","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Contract details (section 2) are internally consistent and accurately traceable to the cited code: the .right > #insrc-newchat + .histchip placement, the newChatPick/renderHistoryMenu signatures, and the .pico 14px icon slot all match the live chat-panel.ts source exactly at the cited line ranges. Two defects found: the repeated \"Errors: undefined when undefined\" entries in 2.1-2.3 are a vacuous placeholder rather than a meaningful \"none\" statement, and citations [[c2]] and [[c4]] — though accurate — are never actually used as inline anchors anywhere in the body (including section 2 itself), only listed in References, so the specific placement and icon-slot-reuse claims in section 2 and 7.1 are not citation-traced as the policy requires.","findings":[{"id":"vacuous-errors-field","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md section 2.1 line 42, 2.2 line 63, 2.3 line 83","message":"All three contract entries (renderHistoryMenu, newChatPick, the #insrc-newchat click listener) state 'Errors: undefined when undefined'. This is not a meaningful statement of error behavior — it reads as an unfilled template artifact, not a deliberate 'this function has no error path' declaration. Given the surrounding Error paths section (section 4) does separately and substantively describe recoverable cases (popup race, host rejection), the contract-level Errors fields should either say 'none' plainly or point to the relevant case in section 4, not repeat a self-referential tautology three times.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:42","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:63","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:83"]},{"id":"unused-citations-c2-c4","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md section 2 (lines 29-31) and section 7.1 (lines 173-177), References section 8 (lines 206, 208)","message":"Citations [[c2]] (chrome markup .right>.histchip placement point, chat-panel.ts:2747-2752) and [[c4]] (.pico 14px icon-slot CSS, chat-panel.ts:2282-2283) are both accurate and verified against the live source, but neither is actually referenced inline anywhere in the document body — a grep for the citation markers finds them only in the References list. The specific claims they would support (the .right/.histchip insertion point in section 2's Surface level line and 7.1's Markup/CSS description, and the .pico icon-slot reuse in section 2.3's precondition and 7.1's CSS description) are stated as bare prose with no [[c2]]/[[c4]] anchor, so a reader cannot trace those claims to their supporting code without already knowing which reference applies.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:31","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:177","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:206","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:208"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2526-2590 (c1, verified: hs/closePops/newChatPick/renderHistoryMenu all present in this range)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2747-2752 (c2, verified: .chrome/.right/.histchip/#insrc-history/#insrc-histmenu markup matches exactly)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2282-2283 (c4, verified: .pico{...14px...} and .pico svg rules match exactly)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2011-2022 (c3 target range, verified newChatPick/new-chat assertions)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2331-2344 (histchip markup test referenced descriptively by c3)"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The renderHistoryMenu/newChatPick/click-listener triplet in section 2 is otherwise well-specified and internally consistent (parameters, pre/postconditions, and the migration steps all agree on the same end state); fixing the two findings above would make the contract fully traceable.","Consider adding the event parameter explicitly to the 2.3 pseudocode signature (currently only named in the Parameters subsection) for consistency with 2.1/2.2's style."]},{"chunkId":"ch3-data-errors","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Data-model call-site citations (dataModelChanges, c3) are accurate and support the byte-identical-payload/no-protocol-change claim. However, the second error case in /body/errorPaths (\"Host rejects the new-chat\") misdescribes the actual mechanism: it claims the rejection is detected via \"webview reconcile() snaps selections back to cur (existing behavior at chat-panel.ts:2562)\" and that the host \"re-echoes run-config/history-list\", but the host's new-chat provider-rejection branch (chat-panel.ts:3309-3313) only calls postRunConfig, which posts a 'run-config' message; the webview's 'run-config' handler (line 2693) does not call reconcile() — reconcile() is only invoked from 'history-list' (line 2698) and 'session-restored'. The comment this claim appears to be borrowing from (line 2696) is about a *rejected open-chat*, a different code path, not the new-chat rejection this error case names. The practical \"state unchanged\" conclusion may still hold, but the stated mechanism and line citation are factually wrong, which could mislead a builder/tester validating this path stays untouched.","findings":[{"id":"errpath-rejection-mechanism-wrong","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md section 4, 'Host rejects the new-chat' error case","message":"The error case claims the host-rejection path is detected via webview reconcile() (cited at chat-panel.ts:2562) and that the host re-echoes run-config/history-list. In the actual code, the new-chat provider-rejection branch (vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3309-3313) calls only postRunConfig (sends a 'run-config' message); the webview's 'run-config' handler (chat-panel.ts:2693) does not call reconcile() — reconcile() only fires from 'history-list' (line 2698, used for a REJECTED OPEN-CHAT per the comment at line 2696) and 'session-restored'. The cited mechanism/line for this specific new-chat rejection scenario does not match the code; it conflates the rejected-open-chat path with the rejected-new-chat path.","evidenceReferences":["vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3297-3313","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2693","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2696-2698","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2562"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/citations/2","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2500-2800","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3295-3324","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1995-2022","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2325-2349","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:5950-5977"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Correct the error-path text to state that a rejected new-chat only triggers postRunConfig ('run-config'), which re-syncs curProv/run-button labels but does not call reconcile() or touch histSel/actSel — the webview's chat-trigger selections were never changed by the click in the first place, so there is nothing to 'snap back'; the real invariant is simply that the trigger selections are untouched because the rejection path never writes to them.","Consider adding one explicit edge case for rapid double-activation of #insrc-newchat (e.g. two quick Enter/Space presses before the first new-chat draft message round-trips) to confirm no double session is created, mirroring the existing popup-race case."]},{"chunkId":"ch4-test-coverage","status":"passed","summary":"The test strategy traces well to the contract postconditions, data-model invariants and error-path claims in ch2/ch3. All line-number citations for both the unit subjects (lines 2011, 2017-2018, 2337) and the integration-level new-chat call sites (229, 648, 659, 735, 792, 869, 1101, 1144, 1573, 3514, 3952, 4431, 4505, 4524, 4619) were verified against the actual test file and match real, specific test/call locations — these are not vague or unverifiable references. The acceptance mapping (ac1-ac5) covers the renderHistoryMenu postcondition (ac1), the new button's markup placement (ac2), its icon (ac3), the click-wiring + unchanged host payload + unmodified host tests (ac4), and a full-suite/tsc gate (ac5). The integration claim that existing env('new-chat') host tests run unchanged is adequately scoped: it names specific existing test line numbers as subjects (not merely asserted) and is backed by ac5's concrete full-suite run, which is a legitimate verification path for a no-new-test, must-not-regress claim given the host-side code is untouched. Two minor LOW gaps found: the ac4 wiring-test description does not specify asserting that the click listener passes the button itself (not hs) as newChatPick's trigger argument, which is the specific mechanism behind the 2.3 postcondition 'button keeps focus'; and the integration subjects list is a curated sample of new-chat call sites rather than the complete set found in the file (more exist, e.g. around lines 1980-1981, 2427, 4635+), though this does not undermine the no-regression claim since ac5's full-suite run covers all of them regardless of enumeration.","findings":[{"id":"f1-focus-arg-unspecified","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md#5-test-strategy (ac4 row) vs #2-contract-details (2.3 postconditions)","message":"Contract 2.3's postcondition is 'popups closed, new-chat posted, button keeps focus', which depends on the click listener passing the #insrc-newchat button itself (nc) as newChatPick's trigger argument (per section 7.1's 'nc click -> stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc)'). The ac4 proving-test description only says the listener 'calls newChatPick' without specifying that the assertion checks the trigger argument is nc, so the 'button keeps focus' postcondition has no explicitly named proving assertion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:88-89 (2.3 Postconditions)","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:152 (ac4 row)","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:177 (7.1 JS: nc click -> stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc))"]},{"id":"f2-integration-subjects-sample","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md#5-test-strategy (integration subjects)","message":"The integration-level subjects list 15 existing new-chat test line numbers, but the test file contains additional new-chat-posting tests not enumerated there (e.g. around lines 1980-1981, 2427, 4635, 4699, 4909-4986, 5204, 5879-5972, 7402, 7472, 8293-8317). The list reads as the exhaustive proof set for the 'host tests run unchanged' claim but is only a sample; the actual guarantee comes from ac5's full-suite run, not from this enumerated list.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:142 (integration subjects line list)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1980-1981","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2427","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:4635"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1990-2022 (regression test for history trigger / newChatPick, lines 2011, 2017-2018)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2310-2359 (histchip markup test, line 2337)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts (grep for 'new-chat' confirming lines 229, 648, 659, 735, 792, 869, 1101, 1144, 1573, 3514, 3952, 4431, 4505, 4524, 4619 are real env('new-chat') call sites)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2520-2600 (bootstrap wiring: closePops, newChatPick, renderHistoryMenu, hs click listener — confirms 2.1/2.2/2.3 contract descriptions and invariant [[c1]])"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider adding an explicit assertion that the #insrc-newchat click listener passes the button element itself (not hs) as newChatPick's trigger argument, to directly prove the 'button keeps focus' postcondition rather than leaving it implicit.","Consider either trimming the integration subjects list to a short representative sample explicitly labeled as such, or widening it to the full set of env('new-chat') tests, so the list's role (named subjects vs. relying on ac5's full-suite run) is unambiguous."]},{"chunkId":"ch5-migration-alternatives","status":"passed","summary":"Migration section (state before/after, 3 ordered rollbackable steps, backward-compat claim) is fully consistent with contractDetails and dataModelChanges — verified byte-for-byte against the current chat-panel.ts and chat-panel.test.ts source at every cited line. Alternatives a2/a3/a4 are soundly rejected against chosen a1 with no contradictions, and the backward-compatibility claim (no persisted/protocol change, shell rebuilt on every panel open) is well supported by the absence of any schema/store change in the contract.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","/body/chosenAlternative","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2510-2600","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2735-2764","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2275-2289","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2005-2022","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2325-2349",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["No blocking issues. Minor stylistic note (non-blocking): migration step 2 bundles both JS wiring and the renderHistoryMenu row removal into one 'rollbackable' unit — acceptable for this small story, but if the build splits these into separate commits, ensure the rollback note still applies to each independently."]},{"chunkId":"ch6-final-consistency","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Reconciling the five completed chunks (ch1 passed/2 LOW, ch2 changes_requested/2 MED, ch3 changes_requested/1 MED, ch4 passed/2 LOW, ch5 passed/0) against the whole document: the standalone scope is honored throughout (ch1), and migration/alternatives/test-strategy all converge on the single stated goal — move new-chat out of the history menu into a dedicated #insrc-newchat button left of .histchip, with the message payload, host handling, store and protocol all byte-identical (ch2/ch4/ch5 agree on this end state; no contradictions found in insertion point, payload shape, or affected test subjects across sections 2/3/4/5/6). One new cross-chunk consistency defect is found here: citation [[c3]] is used at document:line:129 (section 4, 'The history trigger's empty label stays \"new…\" (renderTriggers)') to support a production-code behavioral claim, but c3's own definition (References §8) names only a test-file range (chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018/2337) — the actual renderTriggers function that sets the 'new…' default label lives at chat-panel.ts:2561, inside [[c1]]'s cited range (2526-2590), not anywhere in c3's test-file range. This is a genuine citation-use inconsistency the chunk plan's concern 3 calls out, not a repeat of ch2's unused-c2/c4 finding (which is about citations never anchored inline) or ch3's finding (a wrong mechanism description for a different error case). Given this new MED finding plus the unresolved MED findings already carried from ch2 (vacuous 'Errors: undefined when undefined' fields; c2/c4 never anchored inline) and ch3 (host-rejection mechanism/line citation is factually wrong), the document as a whole cannot be assessed as passed.","findings":[{"id":"f1-c3-misattributed-to-renderTriggers","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:129 (section 4, invariant 'The history trigger's empty label stays 'new…' (renderTriggers)') vs section 8 References line 207 ([[c3]] definition)","message":"The invariant claim at document:line:129 cites [[c3]] to support a statement about the production function `renderTriggers` (which sets the trigger's default 'new…' label). But [[c3]] is defined in References (document:line:207) as covering only `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018` — i.e. test-file pinning assertions, not the production code that implements the behavior being asserted. The actual `renderTriggers` function lives at `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2561`, which falls inside [[c1]]'s cited range (2526-2590), not inside c3's range at all. This is a citation-to-claim mismatch: the citation named does not establish the production-code fact it is attached to, and the correct citation for that fact ([[c1]]) is not the one used. This is distinct from ch2's 'c2/c4 never anchored inline' finding (c3 IS anchored inline here, but to the wrong claim/kind of evidence) and from ch3's 'wrong mechanism for host-rejection' finding (a different error case entirely).","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:129","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:207","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:205","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2561","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2526-2590"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rev-e0821209d94791d0-s1-a1.json","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:1-209 (full document re-read for cross-section consistency)","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:129 (section 4 invariant citing c3)","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:205-208 (References c1-c4 definitions)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2561 (renderTriggers definition, confirms it falls in c1's range not c3's)","checkpoint chunk ch1-scope result (passed, 2 LOW)","checkpoint chunk ch2-contract result (changes_requested, 2 MED: vacuous Errors fields; c2/c4 never anchored inline)","checkpoint chunk ch3-data-errors result (changes_requested, 1 MED: host-rejection mechanism/citation wrong)","checkpoint chunk ch4-test-coverage result (passed, 2 LOW)","checkpoint chunk ch5-migration-alternatives result (passed, 0 findings)"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When fixing f1-c3-misattributed-to-renderTriggers, also re-check whether the OTHER c1 citation at document:line:128 and the c1 citation at line:130 should instead be split: line:128's claim (payload unchanged) and line:130's claim (closePops behavior) both map to logic inside c1's 2526-2590 range correctly, so only the line:129 citation needs correcting to [[c1]].","Once ch2's c2/c4-never-anchored-inline finding is fixed by adding inline anchors, re-verify the new anchors point to claims actually described by c2 (chrome markup placement) and c4 (.pico icon slot) respectively, so the citation-correctness issue found here in c3 is not reintroduced elsewhere.","The alternatives-considered section (7.1-7.4) and the migration section (6) both independently restate the same three-step end state (button before .histchip, row removed from renderHistoryMenu, two tests updated); no divergence found between them — this convergence is a strength worth preserving through any correction pass."]}],"progress":{"status":"changes_requested","phase":"complete","completedChunks":6,"totalChunks":6,"lastMeaningfulActivityAt":null,"activeToolCount":0,"requiresUserInput":false,"checkpointPath":"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/rev-e0821209d94791d0-s1-a1.json","sequence":0,"reviewElapsedMs":0,"unitElapsedMs":null,"observedAt":"2026-11-10T19:47:54.405Z","freshness":"stored"},"startedAt":"2026-11-10T19:30:10.153Z","reviewer":"daemon","model":"claude-sonnet-5","unit":{"unitId":"ch6-final-consistency","phase":"chunk_review","executionId":"6a92a49a-3d21-496a-8faa-f1e47b780364","dispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[]},"plan":{"chunks":[{"id":"ch1-scope","title":"Scope, framework alignment and non-goals","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions"],"concerns":["Whether the standalone framing (no parent HLD) is correctly justified and consistent with the story's actual scope","Whether interactionWithShared being empty is correct given the change touches a shared .pico icon slot and shared chrome CSS classes","Whether openQuestions being empty is justified or whether unresolved design choices remain","Whether the summary's claim that 'only the webview trigger and its pinning tests change' matches the detailed sections later in the document"],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"ch2-contract","title":"Contract details: API surface, markup placement and citations","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3"],"concerns":["Whether renderHistoryMenu, newChatPick and the new click-listener signatures/pre/postconditions are complete and internally consistent","Whether the claimed insertion point (.right, before .histchip) and reused .pico icon slot are accurately described and traceable to the cited line ranges","Whether 'Errors: undefined when undefined' entries are a meaningful statement of error behavior or a vacuous placeholder that should instead say 'none'","Whether citations c1, c2, c4 actually support the specific claims attached to them (location, content)"],"dependsOn":["ch1-scope"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"ch3-data-errors","title":"Data model invariants and error-path coverage","selectors":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/citations/2"],"concerns":["Whether the claimed byte-identical new-chat payload and untouched host protocol are adequately justified by call-site citations","Whether the error cases (popup race, host rejection) and edge cases (empty history, keyboard activation, Escape, CSP) are complete relative to the UI change being made","Whether the invariants-to-preserve list is sufficient to prevent regressions in existing host-side behavior","Whether citation c3 is correctly used to support both data-model call sites and error/invariant claims"],"dependsOn":["ch2-contract"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"ch4-test-coverage","title":"Test strategy and acceptance-criteria traceability","selectors":["/body/testStrategy"],"concerns":["Whether every contract/data/error claim in ch2 and ch3 has a corresponding test subject or acceptance-mapping entry","Whether the acceptance mapping (ac1-ac5) actually proves the postconditions described in contractDetails and the invariants in errorPaths","Whether the integration-level claim ('existing env(new-chat) host tests run unchanged') is adequately scoped as a test subject rather than asserted without a verification path","Whether line-number references for test subjects are specific enough to be checked, and whether any acceptance criterion lacks a listed proving test"],"dependsOn":["ch2-contract","ch3-data-errors"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"ch5-migration-alternatives","title":"Migration plan and alternatives rationale","selectors":["/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","/body/chosenAlternative"],"concerns":["Whether the before/after migration states match the contractDetails and dataModelChanges sections exactly (no drift between sections)","Whether the three migration steps are ordered feasibly and each is genuinely rollbackable as claimed","Whether the backward-compatibility claim is well supported given no persisted schema or protocol change","Whether the chosen alternative (a1) is adequately justified against the rejected alternatives (a2, a3, a4), and whether the rejection rationales are sound and non-contradictory with the chosen design"],"dependsOn":["ch2-contract"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"ch6-final-consistency","title":"Final consistency and whole-document check","selectors":[],"concerns":["Cross-check that the standalone scope declared in ch1 is honored throughout (no implicit HLD/epic assumptions anywhere else in the document)","Cross-check that contract, data-model, error-path, test-strategy and migration sections describe the exact same change with no contradictions (e.g. identical insertion point, identical payload, identical test subjects)","Verify every citation (c1-c4) is used consistently with the claims it supports across all sections","Confirm there is no missing requirement relative to the story's stated goal (move new-chat out of the history dropdown into an icon button left of the history widget) and that alternatives/migration/tests all converge on that same goal"],"dependsOn":["ch1-scope","ch2-contract","ch3-data-errors","ch4-test-coverage","ch5-migration-alternatives"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"Every inventory unit is covered by at least one substantive chunk. Scope/framework units (summary, hldContextSlice, document:line:24 section-1 heading, interactionWithShared, openQuestions) go to ch1-scope. The contractDetails section and its supporting citations c1/c2/c4 go to ch2-contract. dataModelChanges, errorPaths and citation c3 go to ch3-data-errors (c3 is reused in ch4 for its test-pinning role). testStrategy is reviewed standalone in ch4-test-coverage against the contract/data/error claims it must prove. migration, alternativesConsidered (including each of its 4 items) and chosenAlternative go to ch5-migration-alternatives. ch6-final-consistency is the mandatory whole-artifact check with empty selectors, depending on all five substantive chunks, verifying no cross-section contradictions and no missing requirements relative to the story goal.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"ch6-final-consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["ch1-scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["ch1-scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:24","chunkIds":["ch1-scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["ch1-scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["ch1-scope"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["ch2-contract"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["ch2-contract"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["ch2-contract"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["ch2-contract"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["ch3-data-errors"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["ch3-data-errors"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["ch3-data-errors"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["ch4-test-coverage"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/2","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/3","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["ch5-migration-alternatives"]}]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"planning","phase":"planning","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"ch1-scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"ch2-contract","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"ch3-data-errors","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":["resume-rev-e0821209d94791d0-s1-a1-3"]},{"unitId":"ch4-test-coverage","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"ch5-migration-alternatives","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"ch6-final-consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"actions":[{"actionId":"resume-rev-e0821209d94791d0-s1-a1-3","signature":"feac9c6643f4abdf0b4987c7714f9109ad2b3088e5fd6048b06093e5cafd8bc4","operation":"resume","sourceAttempt":1,"resultAttempt":1,"acceptedAt":"2026-11-10T19:37:13.415Z"}],"report":{"reviewId":"rev-e0821209d94791d0-s1-a1","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":4,"LOW":4},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"ch1-scope","status":"passed","summary":"The standalone framing is correctly justified and matches the story's actual scope (a two-file, single-webview-module change with no cross-story contracts). interactionWithShared=[] and openQuestions=[] are both defensible: the change only reuses existing shared primitives (.pico icon slot, chip-matching CSS values) without modifying their definitions, and the one cross-file test surface that renders the same chrome markup (chat-shell.test.ts) still passes under the new markup by inspection. The summary's claim that \"only the webview trigger and its pinning tests change\" is consistent with the detailed sections — the new button's markup/CSS/icon/wiring are all part of implementing that trigger, and the host/store/protocol are untouched. Two minor LOW-level observations are noted as advice, not blocking.","findings":[{"id":"f1-hld-metadata-confusing","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/summary (document:line:7-9)","message":"The Summary section states a concrete 'HLD base run' id and 'HLD effective hash' immediately above the explicit statement in section 1 (document:line:26) that this is a 'Standalone feature — no parent HLD.' Carrying real-looking HLD hash fields for a story that has no HLD is consistent with how the framework self-stamps standalone runs (meta.standalone=true, meta.hldBaseRunId===meta.runId), but the juxtaposition could mislead a reader into thinking an actual HLD artifact was authored and consulted.","evidenceReferences":["document:line:7","document:line:8","document:line:9","document:line:24","document:line:26",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json#meta.standalone",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json#meta.hldBaseRunId"]},{"id":"f2-chat-shell-test-not-mentioned","severity":"LOW","location":"/body/interactionWithShared","message":"vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts renders the same chrome shell (runShell()) and contains an assertion at its 'E202611031bd72813:S001 t4' test that locates 'class=\"right\"' and 'id=\"insrc-history\"' by string index and asserts histAt > rightAt. Inserting the new #insrc-newchat button inside .right before .histchip does not break this specific assertion (histAt is still after the '.right' span open), so no fix is required, but this cross-file shared-rendering surface is not mentioned anywhere in interactionWithShared, dataModelChanges.callSites, or the test strategy's subjects, despite being the one other place in the repo that renders and pins the same .right/.histchip markup this story changes.","evidenceReferences":["vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts:717-724","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2751","/body/interactionWithShared"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:24","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/openQuestions","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2500-2799","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2260-2299","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts:705-734",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider a one-line note in interactionWithShared (even for a standalone story) naming chat-shell.test.ts as a verified-unaffected shared rendering surface, so future readers don't have to re-derive that the index-based assertion still holds after the markup insertion.","Since the exact bubble-plus SVG path data is not pinned anywhere in the LLD (only described verbally), the builder has latitude in the literal icon markup; this is fine for a UI-only change but could be called out explicitly as a deliberately-deferred implementation detail rather than left implicit."]},{"chunkId":"ch2-contract","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Contract details (section 2) are internally consistent and accurately traceable to the cited code: the .right > #insrc-newchat + .histchip placement, the newChatPick/renderHistoryMenu signatures, and the .pico 14px icon slot all match the live chat-panel.ts source exactly at the cited line ranges. Two defects found: the repeated \"Errors: undefined when undefined\" entries in 2.1-2.3 are a vacuous placeholder rather than a meaningful \"none\" statement, and citations [[c2]] and [[c4]] — though accurate — are never actually used as inline anchors anywhere in the body (including section 2 itself), only listed in References, so the specific placement and icon-slot-reuse claims in section 2 and 7.1 are not citation-traced as the policy requires.","findings":[{"id":"vacuous-errors-field","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md section 2.1 line 42, 2.2 line 63, 2.3 line 83","message":"All three contract entries (renderHistoryMenu, newChatPick, the #insrc-newchat click listener) state 'Errors: undefined when undefined'. This is not a meaningful statement of error behavior — it reads as an unfilled template artifact, not a deliberate 'this function has no error path' declaration. Given the surrounding Error paths section (section 4) does separately and substantively describe recoverable cases (popup race, host rejection), the contract-level Errors fields should either say 'none' plainly or point to the relevant case in section 4, not repeat a self-referential tautology three times.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:42","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:63","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:83"]},{"id":"unused-citations-c2-c4","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md section 2 (lines 29-31) and section 7.1 (lines 173-177), References section 8 (lines 206, 208)","message":"Citations [[c2]] (chrome markup .right>.histchip placement point, chat-panel.ts:2747-2752) and [[c4]] (.pico 14px icon-slot CSS, chat-panel.ts:2282-2283) are both accurate and verified against the live source, but neither is actually referenced inline anywhere in the document body — a grep for the citation markers finds them only in the References list. The specific claims they would support (the .right/.histchip insertion point in section 2's Surface level line and 7.1's Markup/CSS description, and the .pico icon-slot reuse in section 2.3's precondition and 7.1's CSS description) are stated as bare prose with no [[c2]]/[[c4]] anchor, so a reader cannot trace those claims to their supporting code without already knowing which reference applies.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:31","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:177","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:206","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:208"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2526-2590 (c1, verified: hs/closePops/newChatPick/renderHistoryMenu all present in this range)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2747-2752 (c2, verified: .chrome/.right/.histchip/#insrc-history/#insrc-histmenu markup matches exactly)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2282-2283 (c4, verified: .pico{...14px...} and .pico svg rules match exactly)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2011-2022 (c3 target range, verified newChatPick/new-chat assertions)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2331-2344 (histchip markup test referenced descriptively by c3)"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The renderHistoryMenu/newChatPick/click-listener triplet in section 2 is otherwise well-specified and internally consistent (parameters, pre/postconditions, and the migration steps all agree on the same end state); fixing the two findings above would make the contract fully traceable.","Consider adding the event parameter explicitly to the 2.3 pseudocode signature (currently only named in the Parameters subsection) for consistency with 2.1/2.2's style."]},{"chunkId":"ch3-data-errors","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Data-model call-site citations (dataModelChanges, c3) are accurate and support the byte-identical-payload/no-protocol-change claim. However, the second error case in /body/errorPaths (\"Host rejects the new-chat\") misdescribes the actual mechanism: it claims the rejection is detected via \"webview reconcile() snaps selections back to cur (existing behavior at chat-panel.ts:2562)\" and that the host \"re-echoes run-config/history-list\", but the host's new-chat provider-rejection branch (chat-panel.ts:3309-3313) only calls postRunConfig, which posts a 'run-config' message; the webview's 'run-config' handler (line 2693) does not call reconcile() — reconcile() is only invoked from 'history-list' (line 2698) and 'session-restored'. The comment this claim appears to be borrowing from (line 2696) is about a *rejected open-chat*, a different code path, not the new-chat rejection this error case names. The practical \"state unchanged\" conclusion may still hold, but the stated mechanism and line citation are factually wrong, which could mislead a builder/tester validating this path stays untouched.","findings":[{"id":"errpath-rejection-mechanism-wrong","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md section 4, 'Host rejects the new-chat' error case","message":"The error case claims the host-rejection path is detected via webview reconcile() (cited at chat-panel.ts:2562) and that the host re-echoes run-config/history-list. In the actual code, the new-chat provider-rejection branch (vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3309-3313) calls only postRunConfig (sends a 'run-config' message); the webview's 'run-config' handler (chat-panel.ts:2693) does not call reconcile() — reconcile() only fires from 'history-list' (line 2698, used for a REJECTED OPEN-CHAT per the comment at line 2696) and 'session-restored'. The cited mechanism/line for this specific new-chat rejection scenario does not match the code; it conflates the rejected-open-chat path with the rejected-new-chat path.","evidenceReferences":["vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3297-3313","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2693","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2696-2698","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2562"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/citations/2","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2500-2800","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3295-3324","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1995-2022","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2325-2349","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:5950-5977"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Correct the error-path text to state that a rejected new-chat only triggers postRunConfig ('run-config'), which re-syncs curProv/run-button labels but does not call reconcile() or touch histSel/actSel — the webview's chat-trigger selections were never changed by the click in the first place, so there is nothing to 'snap back'; the real invariant is simply that the trigger selections are untouched because the rejection path never writes to them.","Consider adding one explicit edge case for rapid double-activation of #insrc-newchat (e.g. two quick Enter/Space presses before the first new-chat draft message round-trips) to confirm no double session is created, mirroring the existing popup-race case."]},{"chunkId":"ch4-test-coverage","status":"passed","summary":"The test strategy traces well to the contract postconditions, data-model invariants and error-path claims in ch2/ch3. All line-number citations for both the unit subjects (lines 2011, 2017-2018, 2337) and the integration-level new-chat call sites (229, 648, 659, 735, 792, 869, 1101, 1144, 1573, 3514, 3952, 4431, 4505, 4524, 4619) were verified against the actual test file and match real, specific test/call locations — these are not vague or unverifiable references. The acceptance mapping (ac1-ac5) covers the renderHistoryMenu postcondition (ac1), the new button's markup placement (ac2), its icon (ac3), the click-wiring + unchanged host payload + unmodified host tests (ac4), and a full-suite/tsc gate (ac5). The integration claim that existing env('new-chat') host tests run unchanged is adequately scoped: it names specific existing test line numbers as subjects (not merely asserted) and is backed by ac5's concrete full-suite run, which is a legitimate verification path for a no-new-test, must-not-regress claim given the host-side code is untouched. Two minor LOW gaps found: the ac4 wiring-test description does not specify asserting that the click listener passes the button itself (not hs) as newChatPick's trigger argument, which is the specific mechanism behind the 2.3 postcondition 'button keeps focus'; and the integration subjects list is a curated sample of new-chat call sites rather than the complete set found in the file (more exist, e.g. around lines 1980-1981, 2427, 4635+), though this does not undermine the no-regression claim since ac5's full-suite run covers all of them regardless of enumeration.","findings":[{"id":"f1-focus-arg-unspecified","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md#5-test-strategy (ac4 row) vs #2-contract-details (2.3 postconditions)","message":"Contract 2.3's postcondition is 'popups closed, new-chat posted, button keeps focus', which depends on the click listener passing the #insrc-newchat button itself (nc) as newChatPick's trigger argument (per section 7.1's 'nc click -> stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc)'). The ac4 proving-test description only says the listener 'calls newChatPick' without specifying that the assertion checks the trigger argument is nc, so the 'button keeps focus' postcondition has no explicitly named proving assertion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:88-89 (2.3 Postconditions)","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:152 (ac4 row)","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:177 (7.1 JS: nc click -> stopPropagation + newChatPick(nc))"]},{"id":"f2-integration-subjects-sample","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md#5-test-strategy (integration subjects)","message":"The integration-level subjects list 15 existing new-chat test line numbers, but the test file contains additional new-chat-posting tests not enumerated there (e.g. around lines 1980-1981, 2427, 4635, 4699, 4909-4986, 5204, 5879-5972, 7402, 7472, 8293-8317). The list reads as the exhaustive proof set for the 'host tests run unchanged' claim but is only a sample; the actual guarantee comes from ac5's full-suite run, not from this enumerated list.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:142 (integration subjects line list)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1980-1981","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2427","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:4635"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/testStrategy","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1990-2022 (regression test for history trigger / newChatPick, lines 2011, 2017-2018)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2310-2359 (histchip markup test, line 2337)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts (grep for 'new-chat' confirming lines 229, 648, 659, 735, 792, 869, 1101, 1144, 1573, 3514, 3952, 4431, 4505, 4524, 4619 are real env('new-chat') call sites)","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2520-2600 (bootstrap wiring: closePops, newChatPick, renderHistoryMenu, hs click listener — confirms 2.1/2.2/2.3 contract descriptions and invariant [[c1]])"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Consider adding an explicit assertion that the #insrc-newchat click listener passes the button element itself (not hs) as newChatPick's trigger argument, to directly prove the 'button keeps focus' postcondition rather than leaving it implicit.","Consider either trimming the integration subjects list to a short representative sample explicitly labeled as such, or widening it to the full set of env('new-chat') tests, so the list's role (named subjects vs. relying on ac5's full-suite run) is unambiguous."]},{"chunkId":"ch5-migration-alternatives","status":"passed","summary":"Migration section (state before/after, 3 ordered rollbackable steps, backward-compat claim) is fully consistent with contractDetails and dataModelChanges — verified byte-for-byte against the current chat-panel.ts and chat-panel.test.ts source at every cited line. Alternatives a2/a3/a4 are soundly rejected against chosen a1 with no contradictions, and the backward-compatibility claim (no persisted/protocol change, shell rebuilt on every panel open) is well supported by the absence of any schema/store change in the contract.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/alternativesConsidered/3","/body/chosenAlternative","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2510-2600","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2735-2764","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2275-2289","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2005-2022","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2325-2349",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-e0821209d94791d0-s1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["No blocking issues. Minor stylistic note (non-blocking): migration step 2 bundles both JS wiring and the renderHistoryMenu row removal into one 'rollbackable' unit — acceptable for this small story, but if the build splits these into separate commits, ensure the rollback note still applies to each independently."]},{"chunkId":"ch6-final-consistency","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Reconciling the five completed chunks (ch1 passed/2 LOW, ch2 changes_requested/2 MED, ch3 changes_requested/1 MED, ch4 passed/2 LOW, ch5 passed/0) against the whole document: the standalone scope is honored throughout (ch1), and migration/alternatives/test-strategy all converge on the single stated goal — move new-chat out of the history menu into a dedicated #insrc-newchat button left of .histchip, with the message payload, host handling, store and protocol all byte-identical (ch2/ch4/ch5 agree on this end state; no contradictions found in insertion point, payload shape, or affected test subjects across sections 2/3/4/5/6). One new cross-chunk consistency defect is found here: citation [[c3]] is used at document:line:129 (section 4, 'The history trigger's empty label stays \"new…\" (renderTriggers)') to support a production-code behavioral claim, but c3's own definition (References §8) names only a test-file range (chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018/2337) — the actual renderTriggers function that sets the 'new…' default label lives at chat-panel.ts:2561, inside [[c1]]'s cited range (2526-2590), not anywhere in c3's test-file range. This is a genuine citation-use inconsistency the chunk plan's concern 3 calls out, not a repeat of ch2's unused-c2/c4 finding (which is about citations never anchored inline) or ch3's finding (a wrong mechanism description for a different error case). Given this new MED finding plus the unresolved MED findings already carried from ch2 (vacuous 'Errors: undefined when undefined' fields; c2/c4 never anchored inline) and ch3 (host-rejection mechanism/line citation is factually wrong), the document as a whole cannot be assessed as passed.","findings":[{"id":"f1-c3-misattributed-to-renderTriggers","severity":"MED","location":"docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:129 (section 4, invariant 'The history trigger's empty label stays 'new…' (renderTriggers)') vs section 8 References line 207 ([[c3]] definition)","message":"The invariant claim at document:line:129 cites [[c3]] to support a statement about the production function `renderTriggers` (which sets the trigger's default 'new…' label). But [[c3]] is defined in References (document:line:207) as covering only `vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:2017-2018` — i.e. test-file pinning assertions, not the production code that implements the behavior being asserted. The actual `renderTriggers` function lives at `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2561`, which falls inside [[c1]]'s cited range (2526-2590), not inside c3's range at all. This is a citation-to-claim mismatch: the citation named does not establish the production-code fact it is attached to, and the correct citation for that fact ([[c1]]) is not the one used. This is distinct from ch2's 'c2/c4 never anchored inline' finding (c3 IS anchored inline here, but to the wrong claim/kind of evidence) and from ch3's 'wrong mechanism for host-rejection' finding (a different error case entirely).","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:129","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:207","docs/standalone/move-new-chat-out-history-dropdown-E20261110e0821209/S001/LLD.md:205","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2561","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2526-2590"]}],"inspectedRe